{
  "description": "Error classification. Rules are tried in order and the first match wins. A rule matches an HTTP error unless mid_stream is true, in which case it matches only an error event that arrived after HTTP 200. Every listed condition must hold: status (one of), status_range (inclusive), type (error.type is one of), code (error.code or error.details.error_code is one of), code_match (regular expression in the portable subset, searched anywhere in that code), message (regular expression in the portable subset, searched anywhere in error.message), header_absent (none of these response headers is present). A rule with a rule name reports it in Error.rule; limit is a regular expression whose first group, parsed as an integer, becomes Error.limit. Connection failures, timeouts and streams that end without their terminal event are transient and are not listed here.",
